<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="86c50455-bb21-56e4-8b87-f90b4271b2e4" activityNameId="e7507a40-7a74-52a2-b27d-4d8d3467033e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Cable, printer cable, without plugs, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Cable, printer cable, without plugs, at plant
This dataset can be applied to describe the production of a typical printer cable to connect to the desktop or laptop computer. The total weight of 1 m of printer cable is 0.072 kg (without the belonging plugs). The information for this dataset is based on weighing, measurements and analysis at EMPA Laboratories. In 2023, only production efforts data are updated. Furthermore, material and energy input are now represented by global inventory flows; UUID: e7bf3741-ebb7-3557-adac-b4063ac626dc
Describes the production of a typical printer cable (connector). Calculated per 1 m of printer cable. Included are the materials copper, PVC, and aluminium with their attributed manufacturing processes like wire drawing or extrusion. The infrastructure is calculated via the proxy "electronic component production plant". Further inventoried are the electricity for the assembly of the connector, the fuel oil, propane and water input, the disposal of plastic and rubber parts, the VOC and methanol emissions created during the processing, plus the road and rail transportation for input materials from the regional storage to the production site. The accumulated hazardous waste is also reported.
Location: The data describes a typical printer cable in 2006. The kind of printer cable is produced by international manufacturers and available all over the world. Therefore a global dataset is justifiable.
Technology: The manufacturing process is represented through plastic extrusion (PVC), sheet rolling (aluminium), and wire drawing (copper).
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Weighing and measuring of materials. Literature for electricity consumption (assembly), emissions and waste.
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: see Geography and Technology
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_e7bf3741-ebb7-3557-adac-b4063ac626dc.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
